---
title: Fill in your instructor profile
description: Which fields the profile asks for, which ones can wait, and the one that can block your course submission.
sidebar:
  order: 2
---

The profile is your instructor record. You can leave it half-done and keep building your course: **the pending fields are only required when you submit the proposal**.

Open it with **Complete profile** in your instructor space, or at [/become-a-teacher/profile](https://ismos.xyz/become-a-teacher/profile/).

## Your account

This part comes pre-filled and you don't edit it:

- **Authentik account** — the one you signed in with.
- **GitHub identity** — empty until you [connect GitHub](/en/profesores/github/).
- **Email**.

## What you write

| Field | Notes |
| --- | --- |
| Name or pseudonym | Doesn't have to be your legal name. |
| Biography | Between **50 and 300 words**. A counter tells you where you are. |
| LinkedIn | Optional. |
| X | Optional. |

## What's asked when you submit the course

- **Country of residence**
- **Years of teaching experience**
- **Whether you have an audience** you share your knowledge with
- **Where you've taught** — Online, In person, University campus, or None of the above (you can tick several)

{% aside type="caution" title="Country really can block you" %}
It's the only field that can stop the submission. We check payment restrictions by country: if you live in a sanctioned country (OFAC), we can't process payments and the form will tell you as soon as you select it. The other fields, at worst, ask to be completed before submitting.
{% /aside %}

## Saving

**Save and exit** keeps what you wrote and returns you to your space. **Go to my course** takes you to the [course form](/en/profesores/crear-curso/). Either way saving is automatic: nothing is lost if you close the tab.

## If you had a profile before

When we verify your GitHub account we may find an earlier profile of yours. If so, we ask you before linking anything:

- **Which profile data you want to keep using** — the current one or the earlier one.
- **Which course draft to continue with**, if there are two.

The contents are **not merged automatically**. We keep a downloadable copy of both profiles and both drafts, and whichever draft you pick stays available in the editor. You can press **Download both versions** before deciding, and **Review the data again** or **Cancel recovery** if you're unsure.

{% aside type="danger" title="GitHub already used by another account" %}
If you see *"That GitHub belongs to a profile associated with another Authentik account"*, sign in with that other Authentik account, or ask support to verify that both accounts are yours. It won't link itself.
{% /aside %}
